01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:56.000
as he accepted it. When police initially began surveilling Yoran's phone calls, they recorded a conversation on June 6 in which Paulus encouraged his son to stick with the story about dropping Natalie off at the Holiday Inn and quote, nothing more. Prior to the arrest of his son and the Calpo brothers, Paulus had explained to them exactly how criminal investigations work and had provided a level of legal advice that went beyond the role of parental counsel. This led to the opinion that he had likely played a part in helping the trio create their false statements and had therefore interfered with the investigation. Paulus admitted to the police that Yoran was a bad liar,

