01:03:56.000 --> 01:04:49.000
but that it was out of character for his son to leave a young girl alone on the beach. He also denied ever telling Natalie's family that he had dropped her at the Holiday Inn, clarifying that his comment related to when he picked Yoran up from McDonald's earlier in the evening. The police agreed this may have been a misunderstanding. On Wednesday, June 15, the Vandersloh's home was searched and two vehicles belonging to Yoran's parents were confiscated and processed for forensic evidence. Nothing was found, but by this point it had been six days since their son's arrest and two weeks since Natalie went missing. On Thursday, June 23, Paulus Vandersloh was arrested on suspicion of complicity in murder,

